This hexadecimal data is the isolated using exiftool the following cmd was ued to automate this extraction:-
exiftool -Comment image.jpg | cut -d ‘:’ -f2 > key.hex

This hexadecimal data needs to be converted back into its original binary format using xxd utility and the cmd:
xxd -r -p key.hex > pvt_key.pem
-r reverses the hex dump while -p tells the program to interpret data as plain hexadecimal. this was then saved as pvt_key.pem.
On using "cat pvt_key.pem" the output is shown as a standerd PEM beginning with -----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY----- and ending with 
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----

Now we need to decrypt the flag.enc using OpenSSL as it has functions for doing RSA encryption and decryption operations using cmd:-
openssl rsautl -decrypt -inkey private_key.pem -in flag.enc

